# {{lb|en|now|_|chiefly|UK|_|dialectal|singular}} A [[man]]; [[person]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014''', original '''1650|author=Francis James Child|title=The English and Scottish Popular Ballads|volume=3|page=355|passage=And after to Callice hee arriued, Like a noble '''leed''' of high degree, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland|collective plural}} [[men|Men]]; [[people]], [[folk]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1838|author=Joseph Bosworth|title=A Dictionary of the Anglo-Saxon Language|passage=Sweet, yes sweet is over (beyond) measure <br>The marrying for the young '''lede''' (people); {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1876|author=(translated by) Henry Morley|title=Shorter English Poems|passage=He said, "Gramercy, liege King, <br>This is to me a comforting: <br>I tell you sickerly <br>For to have land or '''lede''' <br>Or other riches, so God me speed, <br>It is too much for me. {{...}}"}}
#* '''2012''', Yahoo! Canada Answers - Is Jesus God? Did Jesus ever claim to be God?:
